From: Fix HE capabilities has_he flag for newer kernels
Subject: [PATCH] aic8800: fix .has_he = false in RWNX_HE_CAPABILITIES

In newer kernels (6.x), wiphy_register() validates that if a driver
advertises iftype_data with HE capabilities, the has_he flag must be
true. The aic8800 driver sets .has_he = false in RWNX_HE_CAPABILITIES
but still sets iftype_data = &rwnx_he_capa and n_iftype_data = 1,
causing wiphy_register() to fail with -EINVAL at core.c:970.

AIC8800D80 is a Wi-Fi 6 (802.11ax) chip, so HE support is expected.
Set has_he = true to pass the kernel validation.

Signed-off-by: Fix
---
 src/SDIO/driver_fw/driver/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/SDIO/driver_fw/driver/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c b/src/SDIO/driver_fw/driver/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c
index 1234567..abcdefg 100644
--- a/src/SDIO/driver_fw/driver/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c
+++ b/src/SDIO/driver_fw/driver/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c
@@ -XXX,XX +XXX,XX @@
 #define RWNX_HE_CAPABILITIES                                    \
 {                                                               \
-    .has_he = false,                                            \
+    .has_he = true,                                             \
     .he_cap_elem = {                                            \
